{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "20013",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.36,
      "end_seconds": 3.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "Good morning, grab a seat."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 5.29,
      "end_seconds": 10.62,
      "duration_seconds": 5.33,
      "text": "So, um, morning, doctor, sorry about the rush."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 11.77,
      "end_seconds": 14.83,
      "duration_seconds": 3.06,
      "text": "How are things, what's been happening?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 15.5,
      "end_seconds": 23.69,
      "duration_seconds": 8.19,
      "text": "I wanted to get wheezing looked at. My neighbour said I should get it looked at."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 24.58,
      "end_seconds": 27.6,
      "duration_seconds": 3.02,
      "text": "How long has this been bothering you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 28.9,
      "end_seconds": 33.89,
      "duration_seconds": 4.99,
      "text": "It's, It's been going on for about four days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 34.41,
      "end_seconds": 38.09,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "Yes, carry on. How often do you get it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 39.5,
      "end_seconds": 45.16,
      "duration_seconds": 5.66,
      "text": "I, I'd say a couple of times a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 46.87,
      "end_seconds": 50.78,
      "duration_seconds": 3.91,
      "text": "So, have you noticed anything else alongside it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 52.34,
      "end_seconds": 63.35,
      "duration_seconds": 11.01,
      "text": "Erm, it usually comes with yellow phlegm. A sore chest from coughing was there, but it's gone away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 64.59,
      "end_seconds": 68.46,
      "duration_seconds": 3.87,
      "text": "So, any ankle swelling or leg swelling at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 69.93,
      "end_seconds": 74.23,
      "duration_seconds": 4.3,
      "text": "No, no ankle swelling or leg swelling."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 75.37,
      "end_seconds": 79.33,
      "duration_seconds": 3.96,
      "text": "A few quick ones: weight loss or night sweats?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 80.81,
      "end_seconds": 83.76,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "No, I'd have said so."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 84.14,
      "end_seconds": 87.69,
      "duration_seconds": 3.55,
      "text": "I follow. How are your bowels, any trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 89.17,
      "end_seconds": 90.95,
      "duration_seconds": 1.78,
      "text": "Nothing unusual, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 92.27,
      "end_seconds": 94.98,
      "duration_seconds": 2.71,
      "text": "Anything different when you pass water?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 95.64,
      "end_seconds": 97.47,
      "duration_seconds": 1.83,
      "text": "No changes there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 99.32,
      "end_seconds": 102.6,
      "duration_seconds": 3.28,
      "text": "Has anyone ever diagnosed you with something?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 104.35,
      "end_seconds": 111.49,
      "duration_seconds": 7.14,
      "text": "I've had COPD, yes. I just want to get back to normal, really."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 113.27,
      "end_seconds": 114.07,
      "duration_seconds": 0.8,
      "text": "Anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 115.45,
      "end_seconds": 119.89,
      "duration_seconds": 4.44,
      "text": "High blood pressure, for nearly five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 121.97,
      "end_seconds": 126.68,
      "duration_seconds": 4.71,
      "text": "Do you react to any medicines or foods? Any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 127.42,
      "end_seconds": 132.71,
      "duration_seconds": 5.29,
      "text": "Okay, so no, nothing as far as I know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 134.66,
      "end_seconds": 138.02,
      "duration_seconds": 3.36,
      "text": "Okay, have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 139.69,
      "end_seconds": 141.02,
      "duration_seconds": 1.33,
      "text": "No, never."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 141.59,
      "end_seconds": 143.96,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "What's on your current medicine list?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 144.83,
      "end_seconds": 150.18,
      "duration_seconds": 5.35,
      "text": "Tiotropium inhaler. I take it once a day for my chest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 150.65,
      "end_seconds": 151.35,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Ah."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 152.06,
      "end_seconds": 159.07,
      "duration_seconds": 7.01,
      "text": "Erm, you know, I take Dolo, 650 milligrams, when I get the fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 160.07,
      "end_seconds": 162.95,
      "duration_seconds": 2.88,
      "text": "Since when have you been taking it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 164.58,
      "end_seconds": 166.33,
      "duration_seconds": 1.75,
      "text": "About two months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 183.14,
      "end_seconds": 185.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "Anything you do to stay fit?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 187.89,
      "end_seconds": 192.12,
      "duration_seconds": 4.23,
      "text": "I do a yoga class on Thursdays."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 192.91,
      "end_seconds": 196.29,
      "duration_seconds": 3.38,
      "text": "What do you do during the day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 197.04,
      "end_seconds": 201.36,
      "duration_seconds": 4.32,
      "text": "I look after my grandchildren most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 202.46,
      "end_seconds": 214.3,
      "duration_seconds": 11.84,
      "text": "Here are the numbers, doctor. BP is 136 over 87, temperature is 37.4 degrees, respiratory rate 21, oxygen saturation is 94 percent, pulse 98."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 215.08,
      "end_seconds": 216.55,
      "duration_seconds": 1.47,
      "text": "Good, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 218.62,
      "end_seconds": 222.03,
      "duration_seconds": 3.41,
      "text": "Right, let's have a proper look at you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 235.36,
      "end_seconds": 237.13,
      "duration_seconds": 1.77,
      "text": "Yeah, no problem."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 238.81,
      "end_seconds": 240.24,
      "duration_seconds": 1.43,
      "text": "Look straight ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 258.06,
      "end_seconds": 262.63,
      "duration_seconds": 4.57,
      "text": "There are scattered wheezes on both sides and no crackles."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 265.06,
      "end_seconds": 267.81,
      "duration_seconds": 2.75,
      "text": "That's all I needed to check."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 277.36,
      "end_seconds": 290.08,
      "duration_seconds": 12.72,
      "text": "Having listened and examined, I'd lean towards an infective exacerbation of chronic lung disease. It could also be a flare of asthma, so we'll keep that open."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 291.64,
      "end_seconds": 295.61,
      "duration_seconds": 3.97,
      "text": "Ah, what are the odds it's serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 296.16,
      "end_seconds": 308.56,
      "duration_seconds": 12.4,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's an infective exacerbation of chronic lung disease, and we'll know more once the a chest X-ray is back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 310.29,
      "end_seconds": 316.81,
      "duration_seconds": 6.52,
      "text": "Doctor, I did a chest X-ray before they came in, the result's on your screen."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 318.85,
      "end_seconds": 336.38,
      "duration_seconds": 17.53,
      "text": "Right, good, thanks for doing that. Let's get a sputum sample, for purulent sputum. What I'm giving you is prednisolone, 30 milligrams, once a day, for five days. You take it by mouth. It's for flare of lung disease."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 337.54,
      "end_seconds": 339.2,
      "duration_seconds": 1.66,
      "text": "That's simple enough."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 339.72,
      "end_seconds": 345.09,
      "duration_seconds": 5.37,
      "text": "Book a review in two weeks. That's all from me. Any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 345.83,
      "end_seconds": 348.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.23,
      "text": "Alright, thanks, take care."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 348.65,
      "end_seconds": 349.86,
      "duration_seconds": 1.21,
      "text": "Look after yourself."
    }
  ]
}